# CODEOWNERS
# This file defines who is automatically requested for review when
# specific files or folders in this repo are changed.
#
# HOW TO USE:
# 1. Replace @your-username below with your actual GitHub username
#    (or use a team, e.g. @your-org/your-team).
# 2. Adjust the path patterns to match your repo's structure.
# 3. Place this file at ONE of these locations in your repo:
#      - CODEOWNERS          (repo root)
#      - .github/CODEOWNERS
#      - docs/CODEOWNERS
# 4. Commit and push it to your default branch (e.g. main).
#
# SYNTAX NOTES:
# - Order matters: later matching rules override earlier ones.
# - Patterns work like .gitignore patterns.
# - You can list multiple owners per line, separated by spaces.

# Default owner for everything in the repo
*       @your-username

# Example: a specific owner for documentation
# /docs/  @your-username

# Example: a specific owner for a config file
# /package.json  @your-username

# Example: a team as owner for a folder
# /src/  @your-org/your-team
